{
  hexmob: {
    book: {
      patterns: {
        spells: {
          /*dummy_spells: {
            "": "Dummy Spells",
            congratulate: "Remove an entity from the stack, then congratulate them.",
          },*/
          "transform_stimulated_pattern": {
            "": "Transform Stimulated Pattern",
            "0": "Accept the position of a $(l:hexcasting:items/stimulated_slate)stimulated slate$(/l), a $(l:hexcasting:hexmob/stimulated_pattern)stimulated pattern entity$(/l) and a pattern. Try to transform the stimulated pattern entity into the stimulated slate. Cost 10 amethyst dust",
            "1": "If the given pattern has the save stroke as the pattern of the stimulated pattern entity, the entity will discard and the stimulated slate will be written with the very pattern. Otherwise, the entity will lose with 5 heath point while nothing other happen."
        },
        "quench_allay": {
          "": "Quench Allay Patterns",
          "0": "Accept an allay; cost one Quenched Amethyst Shard and transmute it into a quench allay, keeping what it carries.",
          "1": "Accept a quench allay and a vector; command it to fly to that point.",
          "2": "Accept a quench allay and a list of iotas; it casts that spell itself with its own media."
        }
        },
        great_spells: {
          /*dummy_great_spells: {
            "": "Dummy Great Spells",
            "congratulate/great": "Same as $(l:patterns/spells/dummy_spells#hexmob:congratulate)$(action)Congratulate/$, but as a great spell.",
          },*/
        },
      },
      "items": {
        "stimulated_slate": {
          "0": "A stimulated slate looks like a normal slate but actually very different.$(br)Firstly, except written through $(l:hexcasting:patterns/spells/transform_stimulated_pattern)this pattern$(/l), the pattern on it can not be changed. Then, if be a part of a spell circle like normal slates and have a pattern written on it, a stimulated slate will simply allow the media wave pass through without any execution but provide a 10% media discount for following executions.",
          "1": "A mishap will occurred if a circle has two stimulated slate with the same pattern stroke. And there may be some patterns the media discount can't apply, which may be the preserve of nature.",
        },
      },
      "hexmob": {
        "name": "Amazing Mobs",
        "description": "This category contains the records of amazing mobs I collected from all over the world.",
        "stimulated_pattern": {
          "": "Stimulated Pattern",
          "0": "A stimulated pattern is a magical creature that appears like a hex pattern floating in the air. Those friendly creatures can be seen in some amethyst geode. $(br)A hexer called $(thing)Whiteord/$ conducted several researches on them and the discovers can be seen at $(l:hexcasting:items/stimulated_slate)Stimulated Slate$(/l) and $(l:hexcasting:patterns/spells/transform_stimulated_pattern)Transform Stimulated Pattern$(/l).",
          "1": "A stimulated pattern in a amethyst geode."
        },
        "crying_amethyst": {
          "": "Crying Amethyst",
          "0": "These mysterious animals (I am not sure whether they are really \"animals\"), firstly recorded by hexer $(thing)cang_hai_yi_su/$, sometimes appear in amethyst geodes, looks just like a budding amethyst and a amethyst bud on which, have no threaten but will drop some amethyst when killed.$(br)If hit, a crying amethyst may cry out like a ghast. What a horrible sound, I wonder what have those things undergone...",
          "1": "A crying amethyst in a geode."
        },
        "iota_sheep": {
          "": "Iota Sheep",
          "0": "These odd sheep frequent the edges of fields, each carrying a single iota knotted into its fleece. The colour of the wool shifts with the type of iota it holds, and shearing one yields a few $(l:hexcasting:items/thought_knot)Thought-Knots$(/l), each holding a copy of that iota. As for what they eat... wheat, of course!",
          "1": "The iota isn't merely decoration — the sheep obeys what it stores. A vector sets it wandering toward that point; an entity makes it trail that creature; a list of vectors turns it into a little patrol; any other list simply cycles the colour of its wool. Hexers have taken to leaving iotas on these sheep just to watch them steer.",
          "2": "An iota sheep, ready for the shears."
        },
        "quench_allay": {
          "": "Quench Allay",
          "0": "After a surpassing enlightenment, I came to command media and thought beyond the common measure. Inspired by the Iota Sheep, I set out to shape another creature that could bear an iota. Reading through the notes $(thing)Whiteord/$ left behind, I fused a quenched amethyst into a willing allay — and so the quench allay was born. It holds an iota like the Iota Sheep, yet can be steered by spells with ease, and may even cast in its own name.",
          "1": "Related patterns: $(l:hexcasting:patterns/spells/quench_allay)Quench Allay Patterns$(/l).",
          "2": "A quench allay, wrought by the Quenched Amethyst Shard."
        }
      }
    },
  },
  hexcasting: {

    action: {
      "hexmob:": {
        /*congratulate: "Congratulate Player",
